    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Gouldbusk was named for English settler William Gould‑Busk, who bought the Starkweather ranch in 1886.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gouldbusk%2C_Texas",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits twenty miles south of Coleman on Farm‑to‑Market Road 1026 in south‑central Coleman County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.historictexas.net/city/gouldbusk-texas",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the early 1900s, Gouldbusk’s cotton gin ran nonstop, shipping 50 to 100 bales each day to the railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.historictexas.net/city/gouldbusk-texas",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By the 1920s the town boasted a flour mill, theater, several churches, five service stations, a bank, and other businesses.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.historictexas.net/city/gouldbusk-texas",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The community grew after ranchland was sold for farms in 1903, sparking a wave of new settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/gouldbusk-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "By 1940, Gouldbusk had a post office, cotton gin, six businesses, and about 150 residents.",
